1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,455
A kilometer down on the pitch-black ocean floor,

2
00:00:02,610 --> 00:00:04,822
deep-sea cameras cross a literal shoreline—

3
00:00:04,952 --> 00:00:06,436
into an underwater lake.

4
00:00:06,616 --> 00:00:08,956
Waves ripple across its mirror-like surface,

5
00:00:09,005 --> 00:00:11,592
while dark streams pour down the seabed slope.

6
00:00:11,832 --> 00:00:13,767
Its secret is buried ancient salt.

7
00:00:14,529 --> 00:00:17,404
Dissolving beneath the Gulf of Mexico and the Red Sea,

8
00:00:17,542 --> 00:00:20,654
it creates brine up to eight times saltier than seawater.

9
00:00:20,888 --> 00:00:24,427
Too heavy to mix, that dense brine pools in seafloor basins—

10
00:00:24,527 --> 00:00:27,765
trapping toxic methane and sulfur with zero oxygen.

11
00:00:28,010 --> 00:00:30,098
Any crab or fish that strays across the rim

12
00:00:30,128 --> 00:00:31,894
suffers instant anoxic shock.

13
00:00:32,639 --> 00:00:34,655
Yet dense beds of mussels and tubeworms

14
00:00:34,685 --> 00:00:36,611
thrive right along that deadly edge.

15
00:00:36,825 --> 00:00:42,332
In 2022, scientists dove 1,770 meters into the Red Sea—

16
00:00:42,529 --> 00:00:45,289
and pulled mud cores from untouched brine pools.

17
00:00:46,043 --> 00:00:47,467
Without burrowing animals,

18
00:00:47,540 --> 00:00:50,982
those layers preserve a thousand years of earthquakes and tsunamis.

19
00:00:51,202 --> 00:00:53,734
Researchers also test these chemical boundaries

20
00:00:53,764 --> 00:00:56,224
as stand-ins for icy moons like Europa.

21
00:00:57,005 --> 00:01:00,306
Of course, that doesn't prove life exists beyond Earth.

22
00:01:00,572 --> 00:01:03,163
Deep-sea brine pools aren't alien portals.

23
00:01:03,935 --> 00:01:05,638
They're toxic underwater lakes—

24
00:01:05,765 --> 00:01:09,464
recording Earth's violent past and fueling life in total darkness.
